From feead8773657d05060b0d9cdbc345d6f5ec5ca9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:15:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-113295: Out of bounds read in ANGLE

Cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8520817:
D3D11: Fix stale vertex and index buffer pointers

Clear cached D3D11 vertex and index buffer pointers on invalidation
and buffer release, keep state updates atomic on errors, and propagate
vertex array binding dirty bits across shared attributes.

Test: angle_end2end_tests --gtest_filter="*DeletedVertexBufferBeforeInternalDraw*:*VertexBufferOffsetOverflowRecovery*"
Bug: b/568897206
Change-Id: I9f10aae425328e514359c4008fe31f3fa05c2901
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8520817
Reviewed-by: Yuxin Hu <yuxinhu@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>
Reviewed-on: https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtwebengine-chromium/+/783842
Reviewed-by: Moss Heim <moss.heim@qt.io>
